ned in df5d65c29 and failing on the pre-fix 3d525d2bd (D-004: 7 failed); REVIEW-B F1 part 2 (the bless-mark remedy on every refusal), by tests/test_integrate_admission.py::test_an_unbacked_ledger_only_approval_is_refused_by_name (a first-approval refusal carries no remedy) and tests/test_snapshot_readers.py::test_a_released_tier_act_naming_an_unaccepted_verdict_is_refused, in the same pre-fix run; REVIEW-B F2 (TC-278's 'judge' wording), no executable test, by independently checkable evidence: the corrected text in TC-278's method and expected at f01e04ce4, which sitting 003 blessed. Every accepted finding maps, so the gate may render. The gate runs now over the lane's tip, from its base b120c4722, in convergence stance, beside WI-927's checkpoint: trunk has moved since only by docs commits, and WI-927 lands first by the queue, so this lane rebases once, after that landing, before its act. Neither lane touches the other's code or rows, so that rebase owes no further round unless its resolution changes this lane's code or rows, which is checked then.\"\ndocs/decisions/wi-962.toml:43:decided = \"The checkpoint sitting, docs/reviews/wi-962/003-ADJUDICATE-b11fab7.md, judged the amendment set (SR-031, LLR-021 with its new SR-031 parent, LLR-031, TC-021, TC-031) and returned MEANING rows=5, every row [MEANING+BLESS]; its binding reads accepted. Its two minor notes (LLR-021 lists the five answers in prose where LLR-031 defers to IF-298; TC-021's evidence omits the none-found pre-push case) go to status.md's unfiled follow-ups at the landing. No arms map was supplied: the composer generates none and the set adds no new TC. The convergence map for the gate over the checkpoint tip, every accepted round-1 finding to its evidence: (1) the RESYNC entry's file list naming the root README (002-REVIEW-B) -> the corrected list at the entry in project-trajectory/RESYNC_PACK.md (inspection: no README.md in it); (2) the two missed adopter-observable changes (002-REVIEW-B) -> the entry's