wered in the lane: TC-374 drops SR-026 and states its Expected per verified row; the readers' placement recorded for the owner\n    \n    Sitting 003-ADJUDICATE-c0ce587 returned TC-374. Terra's retained session\n    removed the false SR-026 link and rewrote Expected per verified row; the\n    verdict's Dispositions heading moves under another heading. The sitting's\n    design smell (two CPU readers in a shipped module serve only this\n    repository's step) is kept as the accepted plan placed it, high risk for\n    the owner (wi-940 D-009).\n    \n    Bar: both strict lints clean; 3042 passed, 3 skipped; CPU 367.7 s vs 540,\n    wall 60.5 s vs 600, within.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    WI: WI-940\n    Loop-Session: 20261021T045653Z-213020\n\ndocs/decisions/wi-834.toml:93:decided = \"Round 002's F2 (the review-next handoff scenario, the round-001 F3 class in its second round, contested by the builder) went to a dispute sitting, not to another build round; the sitting (docs/reviews/wi-834/003-ADJUDICATE-f95988a.md) ruled R2F2 DISMISS not-worth-cost, and its remedy, rewording the spec's test-list bullet so it promises what the kit's code carries, is added to the lane's spine change list for the checkpoint's Done-when judgement. The finding is not re-raised and later coverage plans exclude it citing that verdict.\"\ndocs/decisions/wi-940.toml:36:decided = \"Build round 1, stage 3 (the plan's P3 to P6, completing the plan's second commit) ran on a fresh kit-builder in headless leg 08: kitlib.winjob gains create_joined_job and job_cpu_seconds over one private _accounting query; check_smoke_budget.py takes --mode only (--elapsed retires), validates cpu-seconds, wall-seconds and max-tests in both modes, selects the job meter on Windows and the getrusage meter on POSIX, refusing elsewhere, and runs the tier with PYTEST_CPU_CAP_JOB=private; docs/stack.ini's [smoke-budget] drops seconds and stamps cpu-seconds 540, wall-seconds 600 and max-tests 3140 with fig lines; the new slow module tests/test_smoke_budget_meter.py holds the platform and outside-process cases. Red before the code: 58 failed, 16 passed, 1 skipped, each at its own missing attribute or assertion. The readings: quiet 332.3 to 338.4 CPU-seconds (54.8 to 55.3 s wall); loaded beside two concurrent smoke runs 421.8 to 426.9 (102.7 to 105.1 s); WSL Ubuntu serial 52.4 and 62.6; the spread 426.9/332.3 = 1.28, under the plan's 1.5 hold, and the WSL reading far under the budget, so the hold did not trigger; cpu-seconds is 426.9 x 1.25 rounded up. Two pulls-forward to keep the commit green: test_smoke_budget.py's ratchet message no longer quotes the retired seconds key (a sliver of P7), and test_cpu_cap.py's already-jobbed probe drops PYTEST_CPU_CAP_JOB from its environment. The coordinator re-ran the affected modules (233 passed, 1 skipped) and the bar (both strict lints clean; 3020 passed, 3 skipped; CPU 355.1 s vs 540, wall 56.6 s vs 600, within). The builder's first WSL command ran from the primary checkout and its sed changed one line of the primary checkout's docs/stack.ini; it restored the exact bytes, and the coordinator found the primary checkout clean. Open for the checkpoint: the two new readers carry no Implements tag (they serve only the budget step, which no SR or LLR covers; LLR-026 is the session kill's), with IF-302's data length, on the spine change list.\"\ndocs/decisions/wi-940.toml:64:decided = \"The checkpoint sitting 003-ADJUDICATE-c0ce587 (accepted) returned TC-374, its one row: (1) a false SR-026 link, (2) an Expected that did not say which condition holds which verified row, and (3), surfaced as a separate design smell for the coordinator or the owner, that IF-302's owner is a shipped kit module, so create_joined_job and job_cpu_seconds ship to every adopter as behaviour no requirement states, while they serve only this repository's smoke-budget step. Its disposition was answered in the lane: Terra's retained sessi